id: regexp/last-index/split/0006
area: regexp
op: RegExp.prototype [ %Symbol.split% ]
in: str:"$" str:"m" str:"a\u000Ab\u2028c"
out: value: str:"3;1:a;2:\u000Ab;2:\u2028c"
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: row M3: line terminators without u: ^ and $ under m on U+2028 and U+2029 (exec, %Symbol.match% and %Symbol.split%), and $ without m before a final LF; Broiler.JS answers .NET's: under m only \r is added to .NET's \n (BuiltIns/RegExp/JSRegExp.cs:931-983 at 1f91b8f1), and $ without m matches before a final LF; a correction of Broiler.JS (JSD-0081); answered by SJL-11.5, Broiler.JS's cut-over to Broiler.Regex
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-regexp.prototype-%symbol.split% spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-advancestringindex spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-regexpbuiltinexec ref:regexpref@1
script: function $s(v) { return v === undefined ? "u" : v.length + ":" + v; } function $a(a) { if (a === null) return "null"; var t = "" + a.length; for (var i = 0; i < a.length; i++) t += ";" + $s(a[i]); return t; } $a(new RegExp("$", "m")[Symbol.split]("a\u000ab\u2028c"))
note: correspondence rows M4, M5, M1, M3: the splitter adds y; an empty match does not split at the start, the end or the last split
since: 31

